# Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) cloud image profile. PINNED TRUST ANCHOR (2026-11-15, agent AT; docs/status/golden-image-results.md s1):
# the checksum file SHA256SUMS is signed (SHA256SUMS.gpg, detached) by "UEC Image Automatic Signing Key <cdimage@ubuntu.com>",
#   D2EB 4462 6FDD C30B 513D 5BB7 1A5D 6C4C 7DB8 7C81
# cross-checked in three places: (1) ubuntu-keyring package (/usr/share/keyrings/ubuntu-cloudimage-keyring.gpg, dpkg --verify clean), (2) keyserver.ubuntu.com,
# (3) wiki.ubuntu.com/SecurityTeam/FAQ ("The Ubuntu Cloud Images checksums are signed with key ..."). The live SHA256SUMS.gpg of noble/current verifies with it.
# BUILD STATUS: fetch + verify are implemented and proven; `build` for an upstream cloud image needs a loop mount or libguestfs (virt-customize) which an
# unprivileged nspawn builder does not have, so the Ubuntu image is NOT built here (see the results document).
UPSTREAM_MODE=cloudimage
# Review 5 L7: pin the dated release directory (e.g. release-20261101), never `current`; `fetch` refuses an empty serial, one older than UPSTREAM_MAX_AGE_DAYS
# (override only with OU_ALLOW_STALE_UPSTREAM=1) and one older than the last accepted ($WORK/upstream-serial.last).
UPSTREAM_BASE_ROOT=https://cloud-images.ubuntu.com/server/noble
UPSTREAM_SERIAL=${UPSTREAM_SERIAL:-}
UPSTREAM_MAX_AGE_DAYS=${UPSTREAM_MAX_AGE_DAYS:-60}
UPSTREAM_IMAGE=noble-server-cloudimg-amd64.img
UPSTREAM_SUMS=SHA256SUMS
UPSTREAM_SUMS_SIG=SHA256SUMS.gpg
UPSTREAM_SUM_TOOL=sha256sum
UPSTREAM_KEY_FPR=D2EB44626FDDC30B513D5BB71A5D6C4C7DB87C81
UPSTREAM_KEY_FILE=${UPSTREAM_KEY_FILE:-}
UPSTREAM_KEY_DEFAULT=ubuntu-uec-image-signing.asc
